From: OpenCode Android Full contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Read fork-event payload before other ptrace requests

Some Android kernels invalidate event payloads after another ptrace request.
Fetching registers before the event's child PID needlessly forces the slow
pending-child fallback, which is especially problematic for vfork parents.
Read the payload first and retain the existing fallback for kernels which
cannot supply it at all.

--- a/src/tracee/tracee.c
+++ b/src/tracee/tracee.c
@@ -588,6 +588,10 @@
 {
 	unsigned long pid = 0;
 	int status;
+	int event_status;
+
+	/* Preserve the event before GETREGSET or PEEKDATA can invalidate it. */
+	event_status = ptrace(PTRACE_GETEVENTMSG, parent->pid, NULL, &pid);
 
 	/* If the tracee calls clone(2) with the CLONE_VFORK flag,
 	 * PTRACE_EVENT_VFORK will be delivered instead [...];
@@ -616,7 +620,6 @@
 	 * the child's own stop when @parent can't get there before the
 	 * child has run, ie. when blocked in vfork(2).  */
-	status = ptrace(PTRACE_GETEVENTMSG, parent->pid, NULL, &pid);
-	if (status < 0 || pid == 0) {
+	if (event_status < 0 || pid == 0) {
 		VERBOSE(parent, 1, "vpid %" PRIu64 ": fork event without the child's pid",
 			parent->vpid);
 		parent->pending_child = true;
